    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file `extract_layout.py` that extracts blocks, lines, tables, or layout elements from a document using a concrete external provider, I will use the Amazon Textract service. This service is identifiable by the `boto3` library, which is the AWS SDK for Python, and the specific client for Textract. I will write the code to use the `analyze_document` method of the Textract client to extract the required elements from a document. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789863221080,
          "start": 1789863219033
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc294f59001rlRK3lSI2EaROl",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc294b76001yF2UWrrM4UxB6L",
      "session_id": "ses_f43d6b499ffehQJC2Kdi9HfhTg",
